Got it, so digits are noise too, only ASCII letters count, and case is ignored. Same two-pointer approach: walk in from both ends, skip anything that isn't a letter, compare lowercased, and return true if the pointers cross. Linear time, constant extra space.

```python
def is_palindrome(s):
    i, j = 0, len(s) - 1
    while i < j:
        while i < j and not s[i].isascii() or not s[i].isalpha():
            i += 1
        while i < j and not s[j].isascii() or not s[j].isalpha():
            j -= 1
        if s[i].lower() != s[j].lower():
            return False
        i += 1
        j -= 1
    return True
```

One thing to flag: with digits skipped, "0P" now returns true, since only the P is left. [[GIST]] skip non-letters, two pointers, O(n)

Sliding window limiter, so I'll keep a queue of only the allowed timestamps, since rejected ones never count. For each request, pop from the front anything at or before t minus window, then allow it if the queue length is under limit, and push it. That's O(n) time and space bounded by limit, not by the number of requests.

```javascript
function allowed_requests(timestamps, limit, window) {
  const allowed = [];
  const queue = []; // timestamps of allowed requests, oldest first
  let head = 0;     // index of the oldest live entry

  for (const t of timestamps) {
    const cutoff = t - window;
    while (head < queue.length && queue[head] <= cutoff) {
      head++;
    }
    if (queue.length - head < limit) {
      allowed.push(true);
      queue.push(t);
    } else {
      allowed.push(false);
    }
  }
  return allowed;
}
```

The `head` index avoids shifting the array, so it stays linear. Space is at most limit entries plus the output.

[[GIST]] queue of allowed times, O(n)

A stack works here. Push each opening bracket, and on a closing bracket check the top of the stack matches and pop it. At the end, the stack must be empty. Anything else in the string gets skipped.

```python
def is_balanced(s):
    pairs = {')': '(', ']': '[', '}': '{'}
    stack = []
    for ch in s:
        if ch in '([{':
            stack.append(ch)
        elif ch in pairs:
            if not stack or stack.pop() != pairs[ch]:
                return False
    return not stack
```

That's O(n) time and O(n) space in the worst case.

